Match: a regular expression over lines, as a builtin with no fork. $(amk.match re,text)
answers the lines of the text that an extended regular expression matches, in order and
joined by newlines, and $(amk.match.file re,path) does the same over a file read whole,
so a parse-time grep over a makefile, a staged module or a plugin directory becomes a
call in this process. The pattern is the first argument, so a comma in it goes in a
define, the way an engine program does; the star twin reads either argument from a
variable. A line is what ends in a newline or the end of the input, and the newline that
ends a file is not a line of its own. A pattern that does not compile is fatal, naming the
function, the pattern and the compiler's reason; a file that cannot be read answers empty
with one warning. match joins .FEATURES.

